This project contains no model weights. It contains code only: patches (`h3_48gb/`) applied
from outside an unmodified vendored copy of another project, and a converter
(`convert_sawfwair.py`) that rewrites a user's own local weight download into the directory
layout that vendored copy reads. Nothing in this repository, and nothing produced by cloning it,
transfers, hosts, or redistributes MiniMax H3 model weights.

MiniMax H3 — the weights `convert_sawfwair.py` reads and rewrites, which you must obtain
yourself — is governed by the MiniMax H3 Community License. That license excludes use,
distribution and display of the model in the United States, the European Union, the United
Kingdom and the Republic of Korea, and imposes notice obligations on downstream redistribution.
This project does not obtain, host, or distribute those weights; you download and convert your
own copy, and you are responsible for confirming the license permits your use before you do so.

The `upstream/` directory referenced throughout this repository's code and documentation is a
vendored, unmodified clone of PipeNetwork/minimax-h3-mlx
(https://github.com/PipeNetwork/minimax-h3-mlx), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
It is not committed to this repository — see `.gitignore` and the README's setup step — and is
never modified by this project; all fork-side behavior lives in `h3_48gb/`, applied from the
outside, so `upstream/` can be fast-forwarded against the original project at any time.

The code in `h3_48gb/`, `convert_sawfwair.py`, and the rest of this repository is original to
